{"toolCallId":"call_58ec16fbaa2e4eabba9872b13f946fb7","title":"Ran grep","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"grep -rn \"REQ-\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/ --include=*.sh --include=*.js --include=*.mjs -l","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"grep -rn \"REQ-\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/ --include=*.sh --include=*.js --include=*.mjs -l | head -20","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["grep"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_5a89e9bcf3254683a9b2f24bdae19b34","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh answers one question but prints a 16-line report to do it. A --quiet flag prints the recommended-level line alone, and the default report stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` exists to answer one question, yet every invocation prints a 12-to-18-line text\nreport: a level line, a score line, a four-line breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A\ncaller that needs only the level parses the second line of that report or asks for `--json` and\npulls `recommended_level` out of a 36-line JSON document for the same inputs. Adding `--quiet` prints\nthe single `Recommended Level:` line and leaves the default output byte-identical, which a line\ncount on both invocations proves.\n\n**Key Decisions**: A separate `output_quiet` renderer, so the default report is never edited in\nplace; `--json` wins when both output flags are passed.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: None beyond `bash` 3.2 or newer, which the script already targets.\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\nEvery invocation of `recommend-level.sh` prints a 12-to-18-line text report: a level line, a score\nline, a four-line factor breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A caller that only needs the\nlevel, such as a scaffolder choosing `--level` or a shell test asserting a recommendation, must\neither parse the second line of that report or request `--json` and pull `recommended_level` out of\na 36-line JSON document for the same inputs. Both routes make the caller depend on a shape it does\nnot want.\n\n### Purpose\n\nGive callers a one-line answer that is the same string the full report already prints, without\nchanging a byte of what the full report prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n\n- Add a `--quiet` option that prints only the recommended-level line and exits 0.\n- Keep the level label in one place, so the quiet line and the default report cannot drift apart.\n- Dispatch the output mode in section 7 of the script, with `--json` taking precedence.\n- Document the flag in the header comment block and in the `--help` text.\n- Verify both output shapes with line counts and a byte comparison of the default report.\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Changing scoring, thresholds or phase logic - the flag must not alter the recommendation.\n- Adding a short `-q` alias - the script's short aliases are `-j` and `-h`, and a new one is a\n  separate decision with its own collision risk.\n- Suppressing stderr - errors and warnings stay visible, because `--quiet` governs stdout only.\n- Changing the JSON schema - `--json` output is untouched by this packet.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the flag, the quiet renderer, the shared level-line helper and the help text |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` writes exactly one line to stdout, in the form `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)`, and exits 0. |\n| REQ-002 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is byte-identical to the current output for the same arguments. |\n| REQ-003 | `--quiet` changes no computed value: level, score, confidence and phase fields are identical to the default run's. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--quiet` together with `--json` emits the JSON document unchanged; `--json` wins and `--quiet` is a no-op for that invocation. |\n| REQ-005 | `--help` lists `--quiet` and still exits 0, and every error path still writes to stderr and exits 1. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- **SC-002**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints `16`, and that output matches the pre-change capture byte for byte.\n- **SC-003**: For `--loc 50 --files 2`, `--loc 500 --files 15` and `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural`, the quiet line equals the level line the default report prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` 3.2 or newer | The script cannot run at all on an older shell; nothing new is introduced | The script already targets that floor and uses `set -euo pipefail` today |\n| Risk | The default report regresses while the shared level-line helper is extracted | Med | Capture three baseline invocations before editing and diff them after |\n| Risk | A caller assumes `--quiet` also silences stderr | Low | Document stdout-only scope and test an error path with `--quiet` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: `--quiet` adds no measurable time; the quiet path is one `printf` and skips the report, so it can only be faster than the default run.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: N/A - the flag reads no input, opens no file and handles no secret; it adds no attack surface.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for identical arguments; the change adds no state, no file I/O and no randomness.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` with no `--loc` and no `--files` exits 1 with the existing usage error on stderr and writes nothing to stdout.\n- Maximum length: `--loc 100000 --files 5000` saturates the LOC and file-count factors at their weight caps and still prints one line, with the same shape as any other quiet run.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A - the script calls no external service.\n- Network timeout: N/A - the script performs no network access.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A - the script is a single pass with no persisted state.\n- Session expiry: N/A - the script has no session.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 4/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~25, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 5/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (the default report is preserved) |\n| Research | 4/20 | Read one script and capture three baselines |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **15/100** | **Level 3 (assigned by dispatch)** |\n\nThe measured score is 15/100, well under the 70-point Level 3 threshold. The packet is authored at\nLevel 3 because the dispatch fixed the level before authoring began, and the score is recorded as\nmeasured rather than inflated to match the contract. The documentation contract, not the change's\nsize, is what the level describes here.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | Extracting the shared level-line helper changes the default report | H | L | Add the helper first, diff the three baselines immediately, and keep the helper's format string identical to the current `echo` |\n| R-002 | A caller expects `--quiet` to hide stderr warnings | M | M | State stdout-only scope in `--help` and in this spec; test an error path under `--quiet` |\n| R-003 | `--quiet --json` silently picks a winner the caller did not expect | M | L | Define `--json` precedence explicitly, document it, and test the pair |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line answer for scripts (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** scaffolder or shell test that needs only the level, **I want** `--quiet` to print the recommended-level line alone, **so that** I can read the answer with `$(...)` instead of parsing a report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Unchanged report for humans (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** developer running the script by hand, **I want** the default report to stay exactly as it is, **so that** a convenience flag cannot cost me the breakdown I read today.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-003: Predictable composition with the other flags (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** caller that combines output flags, **I want** `--json` and `--help` to keep their current behavior when `--quiet` is present, **so that** adding the flag never changes an existing pipeline's output.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. Whether `--quiet` deserves a `-q` alias is deliberately out of scope here; a caller that needs one can ask for a follow-up packet.\n- None blocking. Whether stderr should ever be silenced is a separate decision; this packet leaves stderr untouched.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh answers one question but prints a 16-line report to do it. A --quiet flag prints the recommended-level line alone, and the default report stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` exists to answer one question, yet every invocation prints a 12-to-18-line text\nreport: a level line, a score line, a four-line breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A\ncaller that needs only the level parses the second line of that report or asks for `--json` and\npulls `recommended_level` out of a 36-line JSON document for the same inputs. Adding `--quiet` prints\nthe single `Recommended Level:` line and leaves the default output byte-identical, which a line\ncount on both invocations proves.\n\n**Key Decisions**: A separate `output_quiet` renderer, so the default report is never edited in\nplace; `--json` wins when both output flags are passed.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: None beyond `bash` 3.2 or newer, which the script already targets.\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n\nEvery invocation of `recommend-level.sh` prints a 12-to-18-line text report: a level line, a score\nline, a four-line factor breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A caller that only needs the\nlevel, such as a scaffolder choosing `--level` or a shell test asserting a recommendation, must\neither parse the second line of that report or request `--json` and pull `recommended_level` out of\na 36-line JSON document for the same inputs. Both routes make the caller depend on a shape it does\nnot want.\n\n### Purpose\n\nGive callers a one-line answer that is the same string the full report already prints, without\nchanging a byte of what the full report prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n\n- Add a `--quiet` option that prints only the recommended-level line and exits 0.\n- Keep the level label in one place, so the quiet line and the default report cannot drift apart.\n- Dispatch the output mode in section 7 of the script, with `--json` taking precedence.\n- Document the flag in the header comment block and in the `--help` text.\n- Verify both output shapes with line counts and a byte comparison of the default report.\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Changing scoring, thresholds or phase logic - the flag must not alter the recommendation.\n- Adding a short `-q` alias - the script's short aliases are `-j` and `-h`, and a new one is a\n  separate decision with its own collision risk.\n- Suppressing stderr - errors and warnings stay visible, because `--quiet` governs stdout only.\n- Changing the JSON schema - `--json` output is untouched by this packet.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the flag, the quiet renderer, the shared level-line helper and the help text |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` writes exactly one line to stdout, in the form `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)`, and exits 0. |\n| REQ-002 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is byte-identical to the current output for the same arguments. |\n| REQ-003 | `--quiet` changes no computed value: level, score, confidence and phase fields are identical to the default run's. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--quiet` together with `--json` emits the JSON document unchanged; `--json` wins and `--quiet` is a no-op for that invocation. |\n| REQ-005 | `--help` lists `--quiet` and still exits 0, and every error path still writes to stderr and exits 1. |\n| REQ-006 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- **SC-002**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints `16`, and that output matches the pre-change capture byte for byte.\n- **SC-003**: For `--loc 50 --files 2`, `--loc 500 --files 15` and `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural`, the quiet line equals the level line the default report prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bash` 3.2 or newer | The script cannot run at all on an older shell; nothing new is introduced | The script already targets that floor and uses `set -euo pipefail` today |\n| Risk | The default report regresses while the shared level-line helper is extracted | Med | Capture three baseline invocations before editing and diff them after |\n| Risk | A caller assumes `--quiet` also silences stderr | Low | Document stdout-only scope and test an error path with `--quiet` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: `--quiet` adds no measurable time; the quiet path is one `printf` and skips the report, so it can only be faster than the default run.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: N/A - the flag reads no input, opens no file and handles no secret; it adds no attack surface.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for identical arguments; the change adds no state, no file I/O and no randomness.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: `--quiet` with no `--loc` and no `--files` exits 1 with the existing usage error on stderr and writes nothing to stdout.\n- Maximum length: `--loc 100000 --files 5000` saturates the LOC and file-count factors at their weight caps and still prints one line, with the same shape as any other quiet run.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A - the script calls no external service.\n- Network timeout: N/A - the script performs no network access.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A - the script is a single pass with no persisted state.\n- Session expiry: N/A - the script has no session.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 4/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~25, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 5/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (the default report is preserved) |\n| Research | 4/20 | Read one script and capture three baselines |\n| Multi-Agent | 0/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 2/15 | Dependencies: 0 |\n| **Total** | **15/100** | **Level 3 (assigned by dispatch)** |\n\nThe measured score is 15/100, well under the 70-point Level 3 threshold. The packet is authored at\nLevel 3 because the dispatch fixed the level before authoring began, and the score is recorded as\nmeasured rather than inflated to match the contract. The documentation contract, not the change's\nsize, is what the level describes here.\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | Extracting the shared level-line helper changes the default report | H | L | Add the helper first, diff the three baselines immediately, and keep the helper's format string identical to the current `echo` |\n| R-002 | A caller expects `--quiet` to hide stderr warnings | M | M | State stdout-only scope in `--help` and in this spec; test an error path under `--quiet` |\n| R-003 | `--quiet --json` silently picks a winner the caller did not expect | M | L | Define `--json` precedence explicitly, document it, and test the pair |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One-line answer for scripts (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** scaffolder or shell test that needs only the level, **I want** `--quiet` to print the recommended-level line alone, **so that** I can read the answer with `$(...)` instead of parsing a report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Unchanged report for humans (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** developer running the script by hand, **I want** the default report to stay exactly as it is, **so that** a convenience flag cannot cost me the breakdown I read today.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-003: Predictable composition with the other flags (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** caller that combines output flags, **I want** `--json` and `--help` to keep their current behavior when `--quiet` is present, **so that** adding the flag never changes an existing pipeline's output.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None blocking. Whether `--quiet` deserves a `-q` alias is deliberately out of scope here; a caller that needs one can ask for a follow-up packet.\n- None blocking. Whether stderr should ever be silenced is a separate decision; this packet leaves stderr untouched.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_62a7f4c189614886a9226de9aea8d8bf","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Ordered tasks for the quiet flag: capture baselines, add the helper and renderer, then prove both output shapes. Every task names a file and a command whose output settles it.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: command prints expected output`, for example `T003 [P] Confirm the script parses before any edit ($S). Verify: bash -n \"$S\" exits 0`.\n\n**Shell variables used below**: `S=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` and `P=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the output functions, the globals block and the parser case for `--json` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|--json' \"$S\"` prints the two renderers and the parser case.\n- [ ] T002 Capture three pre-change baselines into `$P/scratch/baseline/` (`$S`). Verify: `wc -l` reads 16 for `--loc 500 --files 15`, 17 for `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` and 12 for `--loc 500 --files 15 --no-recommend-phases`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the script parses before any edit (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET=false' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser with its own `shift` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet\\)' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Extract `format_level_line()` and call it from `output_text` in place of the inline `echo` (`$S`). Verify: `diff` against the T002 default baseline exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` and dispatch it from section 7, after the `JSON_OUTPUT` branch (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` prints 1 line and `--quiet --json` prints the same 36-line JSON document as `--json`.\n- [ ] T008 List `--quiet` in the header comment block and in the `--help` text (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` names both sites.\n- [ ] T009 Document that `--quiet` governs stdout only, so errors still reach stderr (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` with no inputs writes nothing to stdout and exits 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Run the three quiet invocations and compare each line to the default report's level line (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` prints exactly `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`, `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` and `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T011 Run the three default invocations and diff them against the T002 baselines (`$S`). Verify: each `diff` exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Exercise the error paths under `--quiet` (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` alone and `--loc --quiet` each exit 1 with a stderr message and no stdout.\n- [ ] T013 Run the packet validator (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$P\" --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Both output shapes are proven: one line for `--quiet`, and a byte-identical default report against three baselines\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c 'REQ-00' spec.md` reads 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet' plan.md` names the renderer and its dispatch.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` reports 3.2 or newer.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The script still parses. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The success path writes nothing to stderr. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling is unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided` on stderr.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The change follows the script's section layout: globals, helpers, output functions, parser, dispatch. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet|format_level_line' \"$S\"` shows both defined in section 4 and called in sections 4 and 7.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line and exits 0. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The default report is byte-identical to the pre-change capture. Verify: `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` exits 0 for all three captures.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Quiet and default agree on the level for three input shapes. Verify: the quiet line equals the second line of the default report in each case.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] `--quiet --json` still emits valid JSON. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --json --quiet | node -e 'JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0,\"utf8\"))'` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed before the helper is extracted. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` lists every site that renders the label, and no inline copy remains outside `format_level_line` afterwards.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for the changed script. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.sh' --glob '*.md'` names every caller the flag could affect.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before completion. Verify: three input shapes crossed with three output modes gives nine rows, of which the six text rows are asserted.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'password|token|secret' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation still runs before scoring. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc abc --files 1 --quiet` exits 1 with `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A - the script has no authentication or authorization surface, so there is nothing to test.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan and tasks agree on the flag name and on `--json` precedence. Verify: `rg -n 'json.*wins|wins.*json' spec.md plan.md` finds the decision in both.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header comment block and the `--help` text both document `--quiet`. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` names both sites.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] N/A - no README in the repository lists this script's options; the `--help` text is the user-facing contract.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files live in scratch/ only. Verify: `git status --short` lists no new file outside `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/` and the one script.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ is cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls scratch/baseline` is empty or the folder is removed after the diffs are recorded.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n| P1 Items | 19 | 0/19 |\n| P2 Items | 4 | 0/4 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 and ADR-002 are followed by T006 and T007. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet|JSON_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` shows the renderer and the JSON-first dispatch.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Every ADR carries a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*' plan.md` prints `Accepted` for both records.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives are documented with a rejection rationale. Verify: `rg -n 'Alternatives Rejected' plan.md` prints two sections, each with a reason.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path: N/A - the change migrates no data and no API surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds. Verify: `time bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet` is not slower than the same run without `--quiet`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback is documented and exercisable. Verify: reverting the one commit removes `--quiet` and the parser then exits 1 with `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P1] N/A - the packet ships no service and no deploy step; the script is used from the working tree.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review: the flag adds no input parsing, no file access and no network call. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` shows a boolean assignment and a renderer call only.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses: no dependency is added. Verify: `git diff --stat` names one file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md acceptance-criteria.md` names the same flag in all four.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation: N/A - this is a CLI, and the `--help` text is its contract.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` lists `--quiet` in the OPTIONS block.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented. Verify: ADR-001 and ADR-002 in plan.md carry the reasoning a later editor needs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\nN/A - this packet has no named human approver. The dispatch that commissioned it fixed the level and the scope, and that record lives in the packet metadata rather than in a signature row.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Ordered tasks for the quiet flag: capture baselines, add the helper and renderer, then prove both output shapes. Every task names a file and a command whose output settles it.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: command prints expected output`, for example `T003 [P] Confirm the script parses before any edit ($S). Verify: bash -n \"$S\" exits 0`.\n\n**Shell variables used below**: `S=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` and `P=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the output functions, the globals block and the parser case for `--json` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|--json' \"$S\"` prints the two renderers and the parser case.\n- [ ] T002 Capture three pre-change baselines into `$P/scratch/baseline/` (`$S`). Verify: `wc -l` reads 16 for `--loc 500 --files 15`, 17 for `--loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` and 12 for `--loc 500 --files 15 --no-recommend-phases`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the script parses before any edit (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET=false' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser with its own `shift` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet\\)' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Extract `format_level_line()` and call it from `output_text` in place of the inline `echo` (`$S`). Verify: `diff` against the T002 default baseline exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` and dispatch it from section 7, after the `JSON_OUTPUT` branch (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` prints 1 line and `--quiet --json` prints the same 36-line JSON document as `--json`.\n- [ ] T008 List `--quiet` in the header comment block and in the `--help` text (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` names both sites.\n- [ ] T009 Document that `--quiet` governs stdout only, so errors still reach stderr (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` with no inputs writes nothing to stdout and exits 1.\n- [ ] T014 Keep every stderr write on stderr in the quiet path, so a warning still reaches stderr when `--quiet` is set (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '2>' \"$S\"` prints nothing, and `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing on a clean run (REQ-006).\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Run the three quiet invocations and compare each line to the default report's level line (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` prints exactly `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`, `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` and `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T011 Run the three default invocations and diff them against the T002 baselines (`$S`). Verify: each `diff` exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Exercise the error paths under `--quiet` (`$S`). Verify: `--quiet` alone and `--loc --quiet` each exit 1 with a stderr message and no stdout.\n- [ ] T013 Run the packet validator (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$P\" --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Both output shapes are proven: one line for `--quiet`, and a byte-identical default report against three baselines\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c 'REQ-00' spec.md` reads 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet' plan.md` names the renderer and its dispatch.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` reports 3.2 or newer.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The script still parses. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The success path writes nothing to stderr. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling is unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided` on stderr.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The change follows the script's section layout: globals, helpers, output functions, parser, dispatch. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet|format_level_line' \"$S\"` shows both defined in section 4 and called in sections 4 and 7.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line and exits 0. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The default report is byte-identical to the pre-change capture. Verify: `diff` against `scratch/baseline/` exits 0 for all three captures.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Quiet and default agree on the level for three input shapes. Verify: the quiet line equals the second line of the default report in each case.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] `--quiet --json` still emits valid JSON. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --json --quiet | node -e 'JSON.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0,\"utf8\"))'` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed before the helper is extracted. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` lists every site that renders the label, and no inline copy remains outside `format_level_line` afterwards.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for the changed script. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.sh' --glob '*.md'` names every caller the flag could affect.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before completion. Verify: three input shapes crossed with three output modes gives nine rows, of which the six text rows are asserted.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'password|token|secret' \"$S\"` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation still runs before scoring. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc abc --files 1 --quiet` exits 1 with `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A - the script has no authentication or authorization surface, so there is nothing to test.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan and tasks agree on the flag name and on `--json` precedence. Verify: `rg -n 'json.*wins|wins.*json' spec.md plan.md` finds the decision in both.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header comment block and the `--help` text both document `--quiet`. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` names both sites.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] N/A - no README in the repository lists this script's options; the `--help` text is the user-facing contract.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files live in scratch/ only. Verify: `git status --short` lists no new file outside `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/scratch/` and the one script.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ is cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls scratch/baseline` is empty or the folder is removed after the diffs are recorded.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n| P1 Items | 19 | 0/19 |\n| P2 Items | 4 | 0/4 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 and ADR-002 are followed by T006 and T007. Verify: `rg -n 'output_quiet|JSON_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` shows the renderer and the JSON-first dispatch.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] Every ADR carries a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*' plan.md` prints `Accepted` for both records.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives are documented with a rejection rationale. Verify: `rg -n 'Alternatives Rejected' plan.md` prints two sections, each with a reason.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path: N/A - the change migrates no data and no API surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 holds. Verify: `time bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --quiet` is not slower than the same run without `--quiet`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback is documented and exercisable. Verify: reverting the one commit removes `--quiet` and the parser then exits 1 with `ERROR: Unknown option: --quiet`.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P1] N/A - the packet ships no service and no deploy step; the script is used from the working tree.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review: the flag adds no input parsing, no file access and no network call. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` shows a boolean assignment and a renderer call only.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses: no dependency is added. Verify: `git diff --stat` names one file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md acceptance-criteria.md` names the same flag in all four.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation: N/A - this is a CLI, and the `--help` text is its contract.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` lists `--quiet` in the OPTIONS block.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented. Verify: ADR-001 and ADR-002 in plan.md carry the reasoning a later editor needs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\nN/A - this packet has no named human approver. The dispatch that commissioned it fixed the level and the scope, and that record lives in the packet metadata rather than in a signature row.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8f3d32b7e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop